# The Promise of Kahless {4}{B} (cast on turn 5 off two Black Lotuses) comes after Faithless Looting put a Human Warrior
# and a Klingon Warrior into Bot1's graveyard on turn 1. Bot1 may sacrifice a Klingon or Warrior - the artifact Mox Ruby
# is refused, and so is sacrificing both creatures at once (it is "a", one permanent, CR 701.21a) - and sacrifices the
# Klingon Scout Battle-Scarred Survivalist, a Klingon but no Warrior, which also proves the "or" of the rule (CR 612.2).
# "If you do" then returns both creature cards of those two types together (CR 608.2c-f): the Human Warrior Abzan Guide
# and the Klingon Warrior Cha'DIch Investigator. The sacrificed Scout is "other" and stays in the graveyard, and the
# Klingon Warrior Bot2 discarded to hand size on its turn stays in Bot2's graveyard.

